2026-09-27T09:27:25.4379297Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4379561Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4379938Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4380367Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4380493Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4380795Z ================
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4380989Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4381225Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4381720Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4382006Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4382163Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4382560Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4382790Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4382999Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4383565Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4384072Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4385217Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4386008Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4386166Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4386780Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4387554Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4387961Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4388414Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4389016Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4389132Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4480970Z ========
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4481201Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4483218Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4485299Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4485616Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4486245Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4487362Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4488166Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4488900Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4489467Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4490048Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4490192Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4490514Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4490711Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4492094Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4493593Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4494609Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4495831Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:27:25.4496133Z 
